// Launcher config for the nf-core/rnaseq wrapper adapter. Nextflow only
// auto-loads a `nextflow.config` from the same directory as the script it
// runs (here, wrapper/) — not from ../, where the real pipeline's own
// nextflow.config lives with its already-complete docker/singularity/conda
// profiles, resource labels, and container registry settings. Pulling it
// in via includeConfig (which itself resolves ../conf/base.config etc.
// relative to that file, not to this one) keeps this wrapper genuinely
// "the real pipeline, one directory deeper" rather than a re-declaration
// that could drift from it.
includeConfig '../nextflow.config'

// ../nextflow.config and nextflow_schema.json both default
// ribo_database_manifest to "${projectDir}/workflows/rnaseq/assets/rrna-db-defaults.txt"
// — projectDir resolves to wrapper/ (the directory of the script actually
// run), one level deeper here than in the real pipeline. Overriding
// params.ribo_database_manifest here does NOT fix this: nf-schema's
// validator re-derives its own default from the schema JSON's literal
// string when the param isn't explicitly supplied via -params-file/CLI,
// ignoring whatever a plain `params {}` config block already set —
// confirmed by hitting the exact same wrong path on a real run even with
// that override in place. The actual fix is in wrapper/params.json, which
// *is* an explicit override the validator respects.

// Without this, a process like RSEM's MAKE_TRANSCRIPTS_FASTA requests its
// label's full default (e.g. 72 GB, sized for a real genome) and fails
// outright on a smaller machine even though the tiny test genome in
// wrapper/params.json needs nowhere near that — confirmed by hitting
// exactly this failure on a real run. These are the same values the real
// pipeline's own `-profile test` uses for this exact test dataset (see
// ../nextflow.config's `profiles.test`), applied unconditionally here
// since this wrapper only ever runs against that dataset.
process {
    resourceLimits = [
        cpus: 4,
        memory: '15.GB',
        time: '1.h'
    ]
}
